  "term": "carotid artery",
  "definition": "The carotid artery refers here to the internal carotid artery, a major blood vessel whose narrowing from atherosclerosis can reduce blood flow to the brain and affect related retinal circulation. In this context, carotid artery stenosis is linked with disturbances in both cerebral and retinal microcirculation.",
